@startuml
title E03 - Local operation during internet failure
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #2877B5
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #17324D
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F4F7FA
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF1BF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9C6500
autonumber
actor "Resident" as Resident
control "N01\nNode sensing" as N01
control "H02\nHub persistence" as H02
control "H03\nHub time" as H03
control "H04\nHub coverage" as H04
control "H05\nHub rules adapter" as H05
control "H06\nHub resident interface" as H06
control "H08\nHub cloud link" as H08
participant "Home internet / WAN" as WAN
WAN -> H08: Connectivity becomes unavailable
H08 -> H08: Enter bounded reconnect/backoff; retain outbox
Resident -> N01: Create normal household activity
N01 -> H02: Deliver through node/hub transport and commit locally
H02 -> H04: Refresh source coverage from local contact
H03 -> H05: Provide trusted time until anchor expiry
H02 -> H05: Apply committed activity or deadline locally
Resident -> H06: Press I'm OK or Call family
H06 -> H02: Persist explicit resident action
H02 --> H06: Show saved-local / internet-unavailable feedback
WAN -> H08: Connectivity returns
H08 -> H02: Replay pending records in priority/order
note over H03,H05: After time trust expires, absence alerts are suppressed; manual resident actions remain valid.
note over Resident,WAN: Outcome - Local evidence, coverage, routine gating and resident controls continue during WAN failure and replay safely later.
@enduml
